BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (12. INNER vs LEFT JOIN?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (INNER keeps matched rows; LEFT keeps all left rows and fills unmatched right columns with NULL.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 318 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (13. What is a window function?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (It computes analytics across related rows without collapsing them, e.g. rank, running sum or lag.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 285 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (14. What is data leakage?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (Information from outside the training fold leaks into model fitting, making validation unrealistically strong.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 252 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (15. Why keep a baseline?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (A simple baseline gives a reference point and prevents complicated models from appearing useful without evidence.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 219 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (16. Precision vs recall?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (Precision asks how many predicted positives were correct; recall asks how many actual positives were found.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 186 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (17. What does tokenization do?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (It converts text into model-readable token IDs/subwords.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 153 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (18. Why can max length matter?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (Longer sequences increase memory/latency; truncation can also remove useful information.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 120 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (19. What is RAG?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (Retrieve relevant external context and pass it to the generator so answers can be grounded in that retrieved information.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 36 87 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 9.6 Tm 8 TL .960784 .972549 .988235 rg /F3+0 6.4 Tf 8 TL (20. Fine-tune vs RAG?) Tj  T* .666667 .721569 .8 rg (RAG adds external context at inference and is useful for changing knowledge; fine-tuning changes model behavior/weights for a task or style.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
